exports[`get.package.format given: [case5] the help text when: [t0] it is asked for then: the help matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"
🪨 run solid skill repo=.this/role=any/skill=get.package.format

🧮 get.package.format — is this package requireable from commonjs?

usage:
  rhx get.package.format --package js-tiktoken

options:
  --package NAME   the installed package to measure (required)

verdicts (taken from the manifest — the probe is evidence beside it):
  cjs        type is not module            → static import is safe
  dual       type: module + a cjs entry    → static import is safe
  esm-only   type: module, no cjs entry    → use getOneLazyEsmModuleLoader

🟡 a green probe does not mean safe. node 22.12+ loads a synchronous esm
   graph through require(), so a pure-esm package probes green here while
   jest's cjs runtime and older node still refuse it.

exits:
  0  measured — an esm-only verdict is an answer, never a refusal
  1  malfunction — the probe could not run
  2  constraint  — absent args, unknown flag, package not installed

"
`;

